WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.141
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level A one.

2
00:00:05.441 --> 00:00:09.095
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.395 --> 00:00:15.077
Unit seventeen: Time Expressions (at/on/in). Today you will say when things happen with at, on and in.

4
00:00:15.377 --> 00:00:18.006
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.967 --> 00:00:22.362
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:23.217 --> 00:00:23.777
At.

7
00:00:24.783 --> 00:00:26.806
At means used with clock times.

8
00:00:27.417 --> 00:00:28.963
I wake up at six.

9
00:00:29.550 --> 00:00:31.889
Your turn. Say: At.

10
00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:35.293
At.

11
00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:36.645
On.

12
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:39.847
On means used with days and dates.

13
00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:42.078
We have class on Monday.

14
00:00:42.683 --> 00:00:44.755
Your turn. Say: On.

15
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:48.636
On.

16
00:00:49.383 --> 00:00:50.013
In.

17
00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:53.690
In means used with months, years and seasons.

18
00:00:54.283 --> 00:00:55.830
My birthday is in May.

19
00:00:56.417 --> 00:00:58.361
Your turn. Say: In.

20
00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:01.841
In.

21
00:01:02.583 --> 00:01:03.236
Time.

22
00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.517
Time means the hour and minute of the day.

23
00:01:07.117 --> 00:01:07.920
What time is it?

24
00:01:08.517 --> 00:01:10.670
Your turn. Say: Time.

25
00:01:13.533 --> 00:01:14.267
Time.

26
00:01:15.017 --> 00:01:15.681
Day.

27
00:01:16.683 --> 00:01:19.287
Day means twenty-four hours, such as Monday.

28
00:01:19.883 --> 00:01:21.627
Sunday is my favourite day.

29
00:01:22.217 --> 00:01:24.730
Your turn. Say: Day.

30
00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:28.243
Day.

31
00:01:28.983 --> 00:01:29.717
Month.

32
00:01:30.717 --> 00:01:33.099
Month means one of twelve parts of the year.

33
00:01:33.683 --> 00:01:34.986
May is a hot month.

34
00:01:35.583 --> 00:01:37.574
Your turn. Say: Month.

35
00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:41.214
Month.

36
00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:43.253
At 3 o'clock.

37
00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:47.225
At 3 o'clock means exactly at three on the clock.

38
00:01:47.817 --> 00:01:49.259
We leave at 3 o'clock.

39
00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:52.537
Your turn. Say: At 3 o'clock.

40
00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.376
At 3 o'clock.

41
00:01:58.117 --> 00:01:59.176
On Monday.

42
00:02:00.183 --> 00:02:02.694
On Monday means during the day called Monday.

43
00:02:03.283 --> 00:02:04.586
I swim on Monday.

44
00:02:05.183 --> 00:02:08.021
Your turn. Say: On Monday.

45
00:02:10.867 --> 00:02:12.088
On Monday.

46
00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:16.829
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:17.683 --> 00:02:21.973
Visal, when do you get up? Do you say 'in six o'clock' or 'at six o'clock'?

48
00:02:23.083 --> 00:02:33.680
At six o'clock. We use at for clock times: at 3 o'clock, at noon, at night. We use on for days and dates: on Monday, on 5th May.

49
00:02:34.783 --> 00:02:35.680
And in?

50
00:02:36.783 --> 00:02:48.422
We use in for longer times: in May, in 2026, in summer, in the morning. For the morning, afternoon and evening, we use in; but we say at night.

51
00:02:49.517 --> 00:02:50.762
How do I remember them?

52
00:02:51.850 --> 00:03:03.575
Think of size. At is a small point of time, on is a day, and in is a longer period. At 3 o'clock, on Monday, in May. Learn these three phrases first.

53
00:03:04.733 --> 00:03:06.570
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:07.417 --> 00:03:11.053
Grammar focus: Time prepositions: at and on and in.

55
00:03:11.353 --> 00:03:12.575
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:13.283 --> 00:03:14.900
I wake up at six o'clock.

57
00:03:15.783 --> 00:03:17.527
We have English on Monday.

58
00:03:18.417 --> 00:03:20.021
My birthday is in May.

59
00:03:20.967 --> 00:03:28.008
At + clock time, on + day or date, in + month, year, season or part of the day. Say at night, not in the night.

60
00:03:28.750 --> 00:03:32.111
Be careful! Don't say: I wake up in six o'clock.

61
00:03:34.067 --> 00:03:36.206
Say: I wake up at six o'clock.

62
00:03:36.506 --> 00:03:38.157
Use at with clock times.

63
00:03:38.967 --> 00:03:41.480
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:43.233
My Week.

65
00:03:43.533 --> 00:03:45.939
I wake up at six o'clock every day.

66
00:03:46.933 --> 00:03:49.351
On Monday, I have English class.

67
00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:52.726
On Saturday, I visit my grandmother.

68
00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:56.638
My birthday is in May, and school starts in October.

69
00:03:57.633 --> 00:04:00.260
In the evening I read, and at night I sleep.

70
00:04:01.367 --> 00:04:05.183
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:06.017 --> 00:04:08.214
The class starts blank nine o'clock.

72
00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:11.250
A, at. B, on. C, in.

73
00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:16.370
The answer is A: at.

74
00:04:17.517 --> 00:04:19.296
My birthday is blank June.

75
00:04:19.596 --> 00:04:22.181
A, at. B, on. C, in.

76
00:04:25.733 --> 00:04:27.559
The answer is C: in.

77
00:04:28.717 --> 00:04:30.530
We play football blank Sunday.

78
00:04:30.830 --> 00:04:33.694
A, in. B, at. C, on.

79
00:04:37.233 --> 00:04:38.919
The answer is C: on.

80
00:04:40.083 --> 00:04:41.851
Which sentence is correct?

81
00:04:42.151 --> 00:04:47.162
A, I sleep in night.. B, I sleep at night.. C, I sleep on night..

82
00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.874
The answer is B: I sleep at night..

83
00:04:54.017 --> 00:04:56.423
According to the reading, when does school start?

84
00:04:56.723 --> 00:05:00.469
A, in October. B, on Monday. C, at night.

85
00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:05.975
The answer is A: in October.

86
00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:10.516
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:14.627
Write three sentences about your schedule using 'at', 'on', and 'in'.

88
00:05:23.417 --> 00:05:24.836
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:25.136 --> 00:05:40.068
I get up at six o'clock. I have English class on Monday. My birthday is in May. I use at for the time on a clock, on for a day, and in for a month. These small words are important in time sentences.

90
00:05:40.368 --> 00:05:42.089
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:42.983 --> 00:05:47.818
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and time prepositions: at and on and in.

92
00:05:48.118 --> 00:05:52.768
Today's value is punctuality. Be on time for school and for friends.

93
00:05:53.068 --> 00:05:55.778
See you in Unit eighteen. Goodbye!

94
00:05:56.078 --> 00:05:58.475
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

